roviso 2 to sub-section 3 of Section 9 of the RERD Act, 2016 to be heard. Further, you are also allowed to remove the deficiencies, inaccuracies, and submit proper documents online within 5 days of the return of the application. Further, you are hereby allowed to be heard in person or through your representative by the Real Estate Regulatory Authority, Punjab, in the Conference Room, First Floor, Block-B, Plot No. 3, Madhya Marg, Sector 18-A, Chandigarh, on 16.04.2026 at 2.30 pm. In the event of failure to submit a proper reply, non-appearance for hearing, or submission of an incomplete response, the Authority may be constrained to take appropriate action, including rejection of the application for registration as a real estate agent, without granting any further opportunity',2,0,'DirectorIT','2026-04-06 15:16:58.000','DirectorIT','2026-04-06 15:16:58.000'),(45476,220007,'DirectorIT','2026-04-06 15:17:39.000',11043,'REA20260158','','','Authority Desk','In-Complete Application (Additional Information Sought by the Authority)','15ac7786-a35e-46a3-ae19-8befd003dcfd','','2026-04-06 15:17:43.593','','2026-04-06 15:17:43.593',0,'','The application filed by you for registration of the agent is found to be incomplete. After examining the application, observations have been shared with you on your dashboard on the authority\'s web portal. Therefore, your application is being returned with a notice explaining why it may not be rejected, given the deficiencies identified in the observations. You are hereby given an opportunity, as per proviso 2 to sub-section 3 of Section 9 of the RERD Act, 2016 to be heard. Further, you are also allowed to remove the deficiencies, inaccuracies, and submit proper documents online within 5 days of the return of the application. Further, you are hereby allowed to be heard in person or through your representative by the Real Estate Regulatory Authority, Punjab, in the Conference Room, First Floor, Block-B, Plot No. 3, Madhya Marg, Sector 18-A, Ch